-- the racemate and the single enantiomer give different counts, which is the statement Pirkle's title
-- makes: the nonequivalence of physical properties of enantiomers in optically active solvents. An
-- optically inactive solution of the same optically active compound is not an optically active solvent.
racemic-does-not-separate : count-in sp-glycerol (sit-in 30 0 mix-pirkle) ≡ count-in sp-glycerol (sit-in 30 0 mix-racemic) → Empty
racemic-does-not-separate q = transport (λ i → isTrue (eqb 5 ((concat (sym mix-glc-pirkle) (concat q mix-glc-racemic)) i))) unit
